concepts.zh:
## 数据从不离开 GPU

每个粒子是 16 字节的结构体：位置和速度各一个 `vec2f`。所有粒子放在一个**存储缓冲**里。每一帧：

1. 计算 pass：每个线程负责一个粒子，读出、积分、写回；
2. 渲染 pass：顶点着色器按 `instance_index` 从同一个缓冲读取位置，画一个小方块。

CPU 只负责每帧写几十字节的 uniform（鼠标位置、时间步长等），十几万粒子的状态从不往返。

## 一个线程一个粒子

```wgsl
@compute @workgroup_size(256)
fn simulate(@builtin(workgroup_id) wg : vec3u,
            @builtin(local_invocation_index) lid : u32) {
  let i = wg.x * 256u + lid;      // 等价于 global_invocation_id.x
  if (i >= S.count) { return; }
  var p = particles[i];
  p.vel = (p.vel + acc * S.dt) * pow(S.damping, S.dt * 60.0);
  p.pos += p.vel * S.dt;
  particles[i] = p;
}
```

`wg.x * 256u + lid` 就是全局线程编号，和 `@builtin(global_invocation_id)` 的 `.x` 一模一样。因为每个线程只读写自己的元素，原地更新是安全的；如果要读邻居（比如粒子间碰撞），就需要两个缓冲轮流读写。

## 同一个缓冲，两种视图

计算管线把缓冲声明为 `read_write`，渲染管线声明为 `read`。同一块内存创建两个绑定组即可，WebGPU 会在两个 pass 之间自动插入必要的同步。

## 实例化绘制

`pass.draw(6, count)`：每个实例 6 个顶点（两个三角形），共 `count` 个实例。顶点着色器用 `vertex_index` 选方块的角，用 `instance_index` 选粒子。一次绘制调用就画出所有粒子。

## 加法混合

片元输出很暗的颜色，混合模式设为 `src + dst`。粒子密集处颜色叠加发光，而且与绘制顺序无关，不需要排序。颜色由速度决定：慢的偏靛蓝，快的偏琥珀到白色。

## 节奏控制

时间步长 `dt` 限制在 1/30 秒以内，防止卡顿后粒子“飞出去”。在途帧数用 `onSubmittedWorkDone` 限制在 2 帧，避免 GPU 跟不上时命令无限堆积、延迟越来越大。

concepts.en:
## The data never leaves the GPU

Each particle is a 16-byte struct: a `vec2f` position and a `vec2f` velocity. All of them live in one **storage buffer**. Every frame:

1. a compute pass gives each thread one particle to read, integrate and write back;
2. a render pass reads positions from the same buffer by `instance_index` in the vertex shader and draws a small quad.

The CPU writes only a few dozen bytes of uniforms per frame (mouse position, time step and so on). The state of 130k particles never makes a round trip.

## One thread, one particle

```wgsl
@compute @workgroup_size(256)
fn simulate(@builtin(workgroup_id) wg : vec3u,
            @builtin(local_invocation_index) lid : u32) {
  let i = wg.x * 256u + lid;      // same as global_invocation_id.x
  if (i >= S.count) { return; }
  var p = particles[i];
  p.vel = (p.vel + acc * S.dt) * pow(S.damping, S.dt * 60.0);
  p.pos += p.vel * S.dt;
  particles[i] = p;
}
```

`wg.x * 256u + lid` is the global thread index, identical to the `.x` of `@builtin(global_invocation_id)`. Because each thread reads and writes only its own element, updating in place is safe. If you needed neighbours (for collisions, say), you would ping-pong between two buffers.

## One buffer, two views

The compute pipeline declares the buffer `read_write`; the render pipeline declares it `read`. Create two bind groups over the same memory and WebGPU inserts the necessary synchronisation between the passes.

## Instanced drawing

`pass.draw(6, count)` means 6 vertices per instance (two triangles) and `count` instances. The vertex shader picks the quad corner with `vertex_index` and the particle with `instance_index`. One draw call renders every particle.

## Additive blending

The fragment shader outputs a very dim colour and the blend mode is `src + dst`. Dense regions add up and glow, and the result does not depend on draw order, so no sorting is needed. Colour comes from speed: slow particles are indigo, fast ones amber to white.

## Pacing

The time step `dt` is capped at 1/30 s so particles do not shoot off after a hitch. Frames in flight are capped at two with `onSubmittedWorkDone`, so when the GPU falls behind, commands do not pile up and latency does not keep growing.
